From: MOHAMMAD <mohamrib@novartis.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:22:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] tools: q36_target_plan, a small-machine estimator for
 qwen36

Mirrors the engine's auto cap (88% of available RAM, KV reserve, top-k floor),
checks whether the dense trunk fits the CUDA tier's default allowance (the
chain needs it whole), gives a bandwidth-bound decode estimate per token split
into trunk / cached experts / SSD, and emits the environment, optionally as a
PowerShell launch script that keeps any variable the user already set.
Defaults describe a Ryzen 7 5800HS + RTX 3050 Laptop 4 GB + 16 GB; every
bandwidth is a labeled assumption, not a measurement.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
